{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124164","id":4739823718,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGoP4Zg","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124164","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124164.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124164.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124164","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124164/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124164/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124164/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/0c1f8be097f086cb0741c8d1321d337842b559b0","number":124164,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[3.x] Fix CharacterBody 2D/3D BVH performance issue","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is the same fix as #121446 implemented for 3.x for both godot physics 2D and 3D.\r\n\r\nCharacter bodies (PhysicsXDServer::BODY_MODE_KINEMATIC) were incorrectly expanding their AABBs to incorporate next frame motion. This should only happen if CCD is turned on. If CCD is not turned on, all the extra broad phase hits are wasted, since narrow phase will not consider motion unless CCD is on.\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nThis should improve CharacterBody2D/3D performance and performance consistency. In addition to the broad phase cost, the narrow phase is currently being fed excess candidate collisions that are costly to test and discard there.\r\n\r\nCurrent performance may be suffering in circumstances with high velocity, diagonal movement or teleporting.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\nThis fix was made originally for 4.x Godot Physics 2D to close #83835\r\n\r\nThe logical issue also appears to be present in 3.x and it is important to fix this before subsequent fixes are added to improve body waking behaviour (as discussed with @lawnjelly on Rocket Chat). Otherwise this bug risks creating additional performance issues when combined with future fixes.\r\n\r\nI do not have a 3.x MRP to test on for either 2D or 3D. I have tested the godot-demo-projects Platformer 2D and Platformer 3D demos and they work. ","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":1